# Implementation Plan - Update IP Impairment Table Columns

The goal is to synchronize the columns of the "IP Impairments" table in the [WfcSummaryPage.js](file:///d:/ReportGenerator/report-generator-app/src/ReportDetails/WfcPerformance/WfcSummaryPage.js) with those present in [WfcIpImpairment.js](file:///d:/ReportGenerator/report-generator-app/src/ReportDetails/WfcPerformance/WfcIpImpairment.js).

## Proposed Changes

### [WfcPerformance Component]

#### [MODIFY] [WfcSummaryPage.js](file:///d:/ReportGenerator/report-generator-app/src/ReportDetails/WfcPerformance/WfcSummaryPage.js)

- Update the table header in Section 4 (IP Impairments) to include:
    - Profile
    - MOS Before HO
    - MOS During/After HO
    - RSSI (dBm)
    - RSRP (dBm)
    - Handover Delay
    - Packet Loss (%)
    - Handovers
    - Call Drops
    - Attempts
- Update [renderIpImpRows](file:///d:/ReportGenerator/report-generator-app/src/ReportDetails/WfcPerformance/WfcSummaryPage.js#240-266) function:
    - Include logic to fetch data for the new columns: RSSI, RSRP, Handover Delay, Packet Loss, Handovers, and Attempts.
    - Use [getKpiCellColor](file:///d:/ReportGenerator/report-generator-app/src/Utils/KpiRules.js#3-316) and [mapToPass](file:///d:/ReportGenerator/report-generator-app/src/ReportDetails/WfcPerformance/WfcSummaryPage.js#18-22) for coloring.
    - Use [getResultText](file:///d:/ReportGenerator/report-generator-app/src/ReportDetails/WfcPerformance/WfcSummaryPage.js#23-34) to display "Result" (linked to the detail section) for KPI columns.
    - Display the actual count for `Attempts`.

## Verification Plan

### Manual Verification
- Verify the "IP Impairments" table in the Summary page has the correct columns.
- Ensure the "Result" links correctly navigate to the corresponding detail section.
- Verify that the colors are correctly applied based on the KPI rules.
